WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:12.150
95. The Fall and Rise of Pompeii. It's a museum of human suffering. Pompeii, in Italy,

2
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:19.350
was destroyed by a volcano in AD 79. Out of a population of about 15,000 people, more than

3
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:27.310
2,000 were killed. Pompeii was a thriving city. Merchants and traders sold and transported

4
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:33.790
products. Fertile soil meant Pompeii was a good place for farmers. The people who lived

5
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:39.710
there didn't understand that beautiful Mount Vesuvius, which towered over their city, would

6
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:48.190
destroy them. Mount Vesuvius had been an active volcano for a long time. It caused earthquakes,

7
00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:56.070
and in the fall of AD 79, Mount Vesuvius erupted. Mud, stones, ash, and poisonous gases blew

8
00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:02.670
out of it. People in Pompeii tried to run away. Unfortunately, many were killed by the

9
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:09.270
poisonous gas before they could get far enough away. Others died when their houses collapsed

10
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:13.910
under the weight of ash and stone from the volcano.

11
00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:18.430
Pompeii and its people were completely buried by the ash that rained down on the city for

12
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:26.550
hours. It ended up underneath seven meters of ash and soil, completely hidden from sight.

13
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:33.670
Surprisingly, the material that killed Pompeii also preserved it. When it was found again,

14
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:39.030
centuries later, people discovered that the earth had protected the beautiful frescoes,

15
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:45.950
wall paintings, artwork, and architecture of the city. Bottles of wine on shop counters,

16
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:52.190
paintings, and purses. Even people's bodies had been preserved, exactly as they were when

17
00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.870
they died.

18
00:01:54.870 --> 00:02:00.990
It was as though the entire town had been wrapped like a mummy. Today, Pompeii is a

19
00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:07.150
major tourist destination in Italy. It's a great resource for scholars who have learned

20
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:14.350
so much about day-to-day life in the past. It's a sad irony that what destroyed Pompeii

21
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.870
is what has kept it alive for history.
